		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4380&amp;p=32815#p32815"><![CDATA[
<strong class="text-strong"><strong class="text-strong"><em class="text-italics">LATE EDIT... About a minute after typing this, I figured out that I had enabled "DIST SORT" (e.g., distance). I've fixed my problem. I'll leave this post in case this problem ever mystifies somebody else as green as I.</em></strong></strong><br> <br>I was fooling around with the Quick settings (thinking of course that I knew what I was doing). Before long, my channel ordering was scrambled in several of the zones. And... the bottom line of type (the one that has the Zone name and channel number) was suddenly reversed (white text on solid background) and the channel number was replaced by "0 km" ... apparently a distance reading that forever reads "0 km." Of course I reloaded the code plug, but that made no difference (again, of course). I'd like to get back to normal. Any help would be appreciated!<br> <br>73, Randy K7RAN<br><br>P.S. I have two radios using OpenGD77 -- a Radioditty GD77 and a Baofeng RD-5R. It's the GD77 I've screwed up.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6820">K7RAN</a> — Sun Sep 08, 2024 11:17 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
